{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"b0290bbc8a0dda24a3b25afbf4e3112d5ec2c6f36dfe022d41653d21f347f47e","slug":"thermal-wind-balance","location":"/weather_technology/force_balances/thermal_wind_balance.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Thermal Wind Balance","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Kevin Goebbert","given":"Kevin","family":"Goebbert"},"name":"Kevin Goebbert","affiliations":["University of Tampa"],"id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","note":"All non-code content is licensed under CC-BY-4.0","free":true,"CC":true},"code":{"id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","note":"All code content is licensed under Apache-2.0","free":true,"osi":true}},"github":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook","edit_url":null,"numbering":{"title":{"enabled":false,"offset":2},"equation":{"enabled":false},"figure":{"enabled":true,"continue":true}},"keywords":["metpy","python","meteorology","weather"],"copyright":"2026","affiliations":[{"id":"University of Tampa","name":"University of Tampa"}],"settings":{"output_stderr":"remove-warn","output_matplotlib_strings":"remove"},"source_url":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook/blob/main/weather_technology/force_balances/thermal_wind_balance.md","thumbnail":"https://kgoebber.github.io/metpy_thebook/build/thermal_wind_schemat-fd4acb711ddd659db4c7039128aa67a2.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"thermal_wind_balance.md","url":"https://kgoebber.github.io/metpy_thebook/build/thermal_wind_balance-a1ee03661d488d9d2b99aa8a153ae802.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The thermal wind is a combination of the hydrostatic balance and\ngeostrophic balance and explains why winds typically intensify with\nincreasing height (stronger winds from the west) in the mid-latitude\nregions (","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"AZ9Q49MwkQ"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"thermalwind","label":"thermalwind","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. 22","key":"uuED1Bhfih"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"22","resolved":true,"html_id":"thermalwind","key":"cj8YwDoIXG"},{"type":"text","value":"). This balance brings together\nthe relationship between temperature and winds. Cooler surface\ntemperatures mean a shorter vertical distance to a given pressure level,\nwhereas higher surface temperatures would mean a longer vertical distance\nto a given pressure level. This results in strong pressure gradients aloft,\nwhich is in association with the strong jet stream winds observed in the upper\ntroposphere.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"uRIF6uFiYk"}],"key":"A5112V5hLW"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"https://kgoebber.github.io/metpy_thebook/build/thermal_wind_schemat-fd4acb711ddd659db4c7039128aa67a2.png","alt":"Thermal Wind Balance","width":"750px","align":"center","key":"fc7bbdbvv1","urlSource":"../../images/thermal_wind_schematic.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"thermalwind","identifier":"thermalwind","html_id":"thermalwind","enumerator":"22","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure 22:","key":"SmPtPE65y0"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"U1IL31OBY3"},{"type":"text","value":"Visualization of thermal wind balance where in the colder air pressure\ndecreases more reapidly that in warmer air creating a strong pressure\ngradient force that increases with height and is maximuzed near the top\nof the troposphere (near 300 hPa).","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"zs06ugU6xV"}],"key":"TZhjnUyOxI"}],"key":"rF3FkXD4ce"}],"label":"thermalwind","identifier":"thermalwind","enumerator":"22","html_id":"thermalwind","key":"IzMZDZ9RsD"}],"key":"gQVGf1x9xh"}],"key":"kisLeSA1GM"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Guldberg-Mohn Balance (Surface Balance)","url":"/surface-balance","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"},"next":{"title":"Color-filled Plotting","url":"/colorfilled-intro","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}